  "configuration_id": "config_002",
  "reason": "The only completed experiment (config_003, acc=0.573) uses a simple linear PCA (pca_n2000) as the RNA encoder within a multimodal multiprofile transformer-aggregation pipeline. With just one data point, the most informative next step is to test whether upgrading the RNA representation to a learned encoder (scgpt) improves accuracy while holding all other variables constant (multimodal, multiprofile, resnet50, transformer, weighted fusion). This directly probes whether the RNA encoder is the current bottleneck: if scgpt yields a meaningful accuracy gain, it validates investing in richer encoders for subsequent experiments; if not, it redirects attention to the image encoder or aggregation strategy. Expected relative cost: scgpt adds moderate overhead over the near-free PCA, so I estimate roughly 1.4–1.7× the 6.61 GPU hours of config_003 (≈9–11 GPU hours). This is a reasonable exploitation step given 8 experiments remain and the total budget allows a few such mid-cost experiments before needing to consolidate."
}

